From 477860d7ffd989871d75cceb31fdef73af291660 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HRSAstro <hrstacey@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:43:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] snr.fits at the restoring beam's resolution

snr.fits was model / uncertainty pixel by pixel. On a model sampled finer
than the beam neighbouring pixels are strongly anticorrelated, so the ratio
read far too low (12.6 against a true 39.3 on a mock disc; ~3 on REBELS-25's
14.5-sigma source) and carried the error map's artefacts.

It is now the model convolved with the restoring beam -- the restored image
without its residuals -- over the 1-sigma of that smoothed model:
sqrt(diag(K M C M^T K^T)) from the full posterior covariance
(`SingleFit.smoothed_std`, via C = L L^T so K M is never held), plus the
prior systematic as the largest change of the smoothed model across the
measured window (`beam_snr`). With point components the points are added
as the beam at their fitted positions and the error uses the joint
mesh-amplitude covariance (`PointAugmentedFit.beam_snr`), checked equal to
the inverse of the bordered system to 1e-10.

Mock disc: 40.8 against a true 39.3, and 11.1 against 9.6 at a quarter of
the brightness. REBELS-25: peak 10, 8 s. Header: SNRTYPE = beam, and the
beam. No per-pixel version is written. figures/snr_maps_mock.png
(scripts/figure_snr_maps.py) compares the maps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01V4AtTWc5c27eTcL5eRWWt8
